response_role_text:
- Body mass and wing: the two large triangles (red and purple) are arranged so one sits above/behind the square and the other forms the lower body — together they create the triangular sweep of a swan’s back and wing.
 the lower body — together they create the triangular sweep of a swan’s back and wing.
