- Head and snout: a small square (rotated like a diamond) sits at the left end and has a small triangle attached to one side. That pairing reads naturally as a head + muzzle.
 a high central hump and a raised rear, the medium triangle gives the bulk of the torso, and the small pieces/parallelogram fill the under‑body and suggest legs/neck. Those role assignments (head, body, hump, rear) match the expected parts of a dromedary.
